  "body": "At `e3b817b6afc6cd413466d43f11ba31209e034bbf`, the [frozen-span loop](https://github.com/mromidev/claude-animated-shorts/blob/e3b817b6afc6cd413466d43f11ba31209e034bbf/templates/scripts/short_qa.py#L50-L57) only records a span when a later frame resumes motion. If the video ends during a freeze, the final span is dropped.\n\nI ran the current loop with synthetic frame differences:\n\n| Input to the loop | Detected frozen spans |\n| --- | --- |\n| `[1.0] + [0.0] * 12 + [1.0]` | `[(1, 13)]` |\n| `[1.0] + [0.0] * 12` | `[]` |\n| `[1.0] + [0.0] * 11` | `[]` |\n\nThe second case should report `[(1, 13)]`, while the third should stay below the 12-transition threshold. This matters when a render stalls and repeats its last frame through the end of the export.\n",
